{
  "quest.50458106894EDFFF.title": "&6Solar Farm",
  "quest.5F14BE199B3484CF.title": "&bStoring It",
  "task.3EDC5F4A0F29DC35.title": "Fuel Generator or Voidflame Fuel",
  "quest.2F9A9E260BC5061D.quest_desc": [
    "Lava is the first fuel you can pipe instead of carrying.",
    "",
    "Build any lava generator and pump lava into it. One lava lake will keep it running for a very long time.",
    "",
    "The &aMagmator&r, &eOritech&r's &2Lava Generator&r and &eEnergized Power&r's Thermal Generator all get 10,000 FE from a bucket. The &aGeothermal Generator&r from &eIndustrial Contraptions&r makes 320 FE/t from 1 mB a tick, which is 320,000 FE per bucket.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: &eEnergized Power&r's &2Heat Generator&r burns nothing. It makes 25 FE/t for each side touching a still lava source, up to 150 FE/t.",
  ],
  "quest.0532680A316DBF67.title": "Understanding FE",
  "task.2E2AAC08F926D8EE.title": "Power \\&\\ You",
  "quest.666CC5BD7E85A79A.quest_desc": [
    "Not every early generator burns coal.",
    "",
    "Build one of these if your base already has a stable, an apiary or a farm. None of them makes much, but each one runs on something you were producing anyway:",
    "",
    "- &aHorse Powered Generator&r: 80 FE/t with an animal walking the mill and a redstone signal.",
    "",
    "- &aHoney Generator&r: 60 FE/t from Honey, using 2 mB a tick.",
    "",
    "- &aBiomass Burner&r: burns Biomass from your &eAgritech: Evolved&r farms.",
  ],
  "task.683E41E7DAE795CA.title": "Any Energy Storage Block",
  "quest.6F54FA28ABED5FDB.title": "&cGoing Nuclear",
  "task.29DAAFF53D9E9531.title": "Late Game Options",
  "quest.2706305DE6477D21.quest_desc": [
    "The two biggest generators in the pack both start with a Nether Star.",
    "",
    "Build a &aFusion Controller&r or a Nitro Reactor. Either one will run everything you have built so far, and a fusion plant keeps growing after that.",
    "",
    "A &eNautec&r fusion plant makes 20,000 FE/t with a 3-wide chamber and up to 300,000 FE/t fully upgraded, but it needs 5,000,000 AP of laser power to ignite. A Nitro Reactor from &ePowah&r makes up to 64,000 FE/t.",
  ],
  "quest.2F9A9E260BC5061D.title": "&cRunning Hot",
  "quest.754048401D3A6A7B.title": "Power \\&\\ You",
  "quest.339B63DF5067A4F4.title": "&bKeeping It Cool",
  "quest.0C006EE92B11ED21.quest_desc": [
    "A few mods run on power that isn't FE at all, and most of them only convert one way:",
    "",
    "- &eNautec&r: its machines run on laser beams measured in AP. The &aBacterial Fuel Cell&r makes AP, and the &2Energy Converter&r turns FE into AP but never back.",
    "",
    "- &eApplied Energistics 2&r: the &aCrystal Resonance Generator&r makes 20 AE/t inside an ME network. A &2Flux Accessor&r from &eApplied Flux&r sends network energy back out as FE.",
    "",
    "- &eModular Force Field System&r: the &aCoercion Deriver&r turns FE into Fortron to power force fields.",
  ],
  "quest.5FC6E8021F428789.title": "&5Eclipse Ember",
  "task.493B10CDEA467DA4.title": "Any Lava Generator",
  "quest.6F54FA28ABED5FDB.quest_desc": [
    "When fuel stops keeping up, split atoms instead.",
    "",
    "Build a reactor. Each reactor mod in the pack has its own chapter covering the build in detail, and the next page compares them.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "- &eColossal Reactors&r: a &aReactor&r you design yourself, which never makes less than 500 FE/t and can't melt down here. Feed its steam to turbines or an &eOritech&r Steam Engine.",
    "",
    "- &eIndustrial Contraptions&r: the &aNuclear Reactor&r. One &2Quad Uranium Fuel Rod&r alone makes 10,240 FE/t, and the reactor explodes when its heat reaches 100%.",
    "",
    "- &eOritech&r: the &aFission Reactor&r, up to 16 blocks across. It goes critical after 400 unstable ticks.",
    "",
    "- &ePowah&r: the &aReactor&r makes 2,560 FE/t at Niotic and 12,800 at Spirited.",
    "",
    "&cWarning&r: an Industrial Contraptions meltdown ignores claimed chunks.",
  ],
  "quest.677873EA54068604.quest_desc": [
    "Every power chain starts by setting something on fire.",
    "",
    "Build any fuel generator and feed it coal, charcoal or wood. It needs topping up, but it gets your first machines running on day one.",
    "",
    "A piece of coal is worth very different amounts depending on where you burn it:",
    "",
    "- &eIndustrial Contraptions&r &aBasic Generator&r: 320 FE/t, 512,000 FE per coal.",
    "",
    "- &eJust Dire Things&r &aSimple Coal Generator&r: 160 FE/t, 64,000 FE per coal.",
    "",
    "- &eOritech&r &aBasic Generator&r: 64 FE/t, 102,400 FE per coal.",
    "",
    "- &ePowah&r &aFurnator&r: 16 FE/t at Starter, 48,000 FE per coal.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: the Industrial Contraptions generator keeps burning when its buffer is full, so give it somewhere to send its power.",
  ],
  "quest.49E157E9B5237314.quest_desc": [
    "Nearly every end-game generator needs a &aNether Star&r somewhere in its recipe, either directly or through Antimatter, Beacons or Nitro Crystals.",
    "",
    "In return, one solar panel makes 16,000 FE/t, a Nitro Reactor 64,000, and a fusion plant up to 300,000.",
  ],
  "quest.5BDF75F1F09E9C22.quest_desc": [
    "Power has to get from where it is made to where it is used.",
    "",
    "Craft any energy cable, conduit or pipe. Every one of them has a limit on how much it carries each tick, and anything past that limit waits.",
    "",
    "&eIndustrial Contraptions&r cables are the exception. Push more through them than their tier allows and they burn out.",
    "",
    "&ePowah&r's &aEnder Cells&r and &2Ender Gates&r skip the cable entirely and move power wirelessly between linked blocks.",
  ],
  "quest.339B63DF5067A4F4.quest_desc": [
    "&ePowah&r's &2Thermo Generator&r and its Reactor both need a liquid coolant, and in this pack water doesn't work.",
    "",
    "Fill a bucket with &aIndustrial Coolant&r, the only liquid they accept. Drop a &2Dry Ice&r onto a still water source block and that block turns into coolant, one block per Dry Ice.",
    "",
    "A Thermo Generator also needs heat under it. A Hardened one makes 64 FE/t over lava and up to 256 over the hottest blocks in the pack. It uses 1 mB of coolant every two seconds, so one bucket lasts about half an hour.",
    "{@pagebreak}",
    "Solid coolants are unchanged. Ice, Blue Ice and Dry Ice still go in a Reactor's solid coolant slot, and &eAuroral&r's &2Shimmering Ice&r works there too, with the same values as Dry Ice.",
    "",
    "Industrial Coolant also works as a heat sink inside a &eColossal Reactors&r reactor, where it gives more than twice the energy of water.",
    "",
    "[\"\", {\"text\": \"Coolant, Steam and Fuel\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,ftb:power,ftb:coolant_and_fuel.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Coolant, Steam and Fuel guide page\"}}, \" lists every heat source and coolant.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.5FC6E8021F428789.quest_desc": [
    "&eJust Dire Things&r saves its best fuel for last.",
    "",
    "Refine a bucket of &aEclipse Ember Fuel&r. It needs the highest tier of Goo, so it is the hardest fuel in the pack to reach.",
    "",
    "In a Simple Fuel Generator it makes 18,080 FE/t, and one bucket lasts 50 seconds, which is 18,080,000 FE.",
    "",
    "&ePowah&r's Nitro &2Furnator&r is the other end-game burner, at 4,096 FE/t from any furnace fuel.",
  ],
  "quest.379AF010B6BB7ECA.title": "&6Brighter Panels",
  "task.4CBB57AF9D47AD33.title": "Any Early Fuel Generator",
  "quest.379AF010B6BB7ECA.quest_desc": [
    "A roof of early panels keeps the lights on, but it won't run a factory.",
    "",
    "Upgrade to a mid-game solar panel. The best of them make eight times what an early panel does.",
    "",
    "An &aMV Solar Panel&r makes 256 FE/t, and &eEnergized Power&r's Tier IV and Tier V make 256 and 512. &eOritech&r's &2Big Solar Panel&r starts at 128 RF/t and grows with the Machine Cores you build into it.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: an &eEnergized Power&r Tier IV panel holds only 256 FE, so connect it straight to storage.",
  ],
  "quest.6393AAFA09F46A77.title": "&6Here Comes the Sun",
  "quest.1A964E72CA3B398D.title": "&6Second Sun",
  "quest.754048401D3A6A7B.quest_desc": [
    "Nearly every machine in this pack runs on the same power, whether a mod calls it &bRF&r or &bFE&r.",
    "",
    "This chapter sorts the pack's generators into four tiers, from the first coal burner to the end-game reactors. Each row is a tier, and each column is one way of making power:",
    "",
    "- &3Fuel&r: burn something and get power back.",
    "",
    "- &3Heat&r: lava, coolant, reactors and fusion.",
    "",
    "- &3Sun&r: solar panels, which only need open sky.",
    "",
    "[\"\", {\"text\": \"Power Generation Changes\", \"color\": \"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"click_event\": {\"action\": \"custom\", \"id\": \"ftbquests:docs\", \"payload\": {\"location\": \"guideme,ftb:power,ftb:index.md\"}}, \"hover_event\": {\"action\": \"show_text\", \"value\": \"Open the Power Generation Changes guide\"}}, \" lists every generator number the pack changed.\"]",
  ],
  "quest.504D47A4397ED4C1.title": "&cHigh Octane",
  "task.17E154E7B81EB1F6.title": "Eclipse Ember Fuel or a Nitro Burner",
  "quest.504D47A4397ED4C1.quest_desc": [
    "Oil changes what a fuel generator can do.",
    "",
    "Build &eOritech&r's &aFuel Generator&r, or refine &2Voidflame Fuel&r for your Simple Fuel Generator. Either one makes thousands of FE/t from a single block.",
    "",
    "The Fuel Generator makes 8,192 RF/t from crude oil, diesel or turbofuel. Better fuels last longer at the same output. A bucket of crude oil gives 1,638,400 RF and a bucket of turbofuel 26,214,400.",
    "",
    "Voidflame Fuel makes 5,280 FE/t in the Simple Fuel Generator, which burns 1 mB a tick.",
  ],
  "quest.35C4B2EA0D7FB8CB.title": "&aEarly Game",
  "quest.6393AAFA09F46A77.quest_desc": [
    "Solar is the lazy answer, and there is nothing wrong with that.",
    "",
    "Place any solar panel under open sky. It never needs feeding and never needs a fuel line, so it is the easiest power to leave running.",
    "",
    "Early panels are small: 32 FE/t from an &aLV Solar Panel&r or an &eLTX Industries&r Solar Panel, 16 from a Basic &ePowah&r panel and 64 from &eEnergized Power&r's Tier III. They stop at night, and anything solid overhead blocks them.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: most mods craft each tier of panel from the tier below it, so the panels you place now won't go to waste.",
  ],
  "task.1B9EDDD730B8EB3E.title": "Fusion Controller or Nitro Reactor",
  "quest.35C4B2EA0D7FB8CB.quest_desc": [
    "Early generators are built from vanilla materials and your first ores, and none of them needs another machine to make its parts.",
    "",
    "Expect 16 to 320 FE/t from one block. The &aBasic Generator&r from &eIndustrial Contraptions&r tops this row at 320 FE/t, and so does its lava twin, the &2Geothermal Generator&r.",
  ],
  "task.7883DDD837E876A4.title": "Mid Game Options",
  "quest.50458106894EDFFF.quest_desc": [
    "Thousands of FE/t from one block, and it still never needs feeding.",
    "",
    "Build a late-game solar panel. The &aHV Solar Panel&r takes &2Iridium Circuits&r, and &eEnergized Power&r's Tier VI takes three Beacons.",
    "",
    "The HV panel makes 2,048 FE/t and Tier VI makes 4,096. &ePowah&r's Niotic and Spirited panels make only 128 and 256, but they need nothing rarer than Diamonds and Emeralds.",
  ],
  "task.482EC56673B12AA2.title": "End Game Options",
  "quest.1BF4810083FE3046.quest_desc": [
    "Mid-game generators need parts made in other machines, such as the &ePowah&r &aEnergizing Orb&r, and several need a trip to the Nether for blaze.",
    "",
    "The best single blocks here make up to 960 FE/t, and the first coolant-fed generators come online.",
  ],
  "quest.5BDF75F1F09E9C22.title": "&aMoving It",
  "quest.677873EA54068604.title": "&6Burning Things",
  "task.6AE9CBE1EAAE4F72.title": "Early Game Options",
  "quest.7E4532B9052F0BEC.title": "&dLate Game",
  "quest.2706305DE6477D21.title": "&dStar Power",
  "task.5772804405C79E5C.title": "Any Mid-Game Fuel Generator",
  "quest.49E157E9B5237314.title": "&6End Game",
  "quest.7E4532B9052F0BEC.quest_desc": [
    "Late-game generators need rarer materials: &aIridium&r, Niotic and Spirited Crystals, oil, End materials and uranium.",
    "",
    "One block now makes thousands of FE/t, and a reactor makes tens of thousands.",
  ],
  "task.3EC6053B7A8B946E.title": "Any Late-Game Solar Panel",
  "quest.1BF4810083FE3046.title": "&bMid Game",
  "task.0F9F80BE3C6A92D6.title": "Any Mid-Game Solar Panel",
  "quest.0532680A316DBF67.quest_desc": [
    "FE and RF are the same thing, so a generator from one mod will run a machine from any other.",
    "",
    "What differs is how much power a block takes in one tick. &eIndustrial Contraptions&r machines and cables each have a voltage tier, from LV at 1,024 FE/t up to IV at 262,144 FE/t.",
    "",
    "Push more than that through its own cables and the cable burns out, and a machine fed a higher tier than its own burns out too until you right-click it with a &aFuse&r. Power arriving through another mod's cables is only held back, never burnt.",
    "",
    "&eNote&r: check a machine's tier before connecting a bigger Industrial Contraptions cable to it.",
  ],
  "quest.0C006EE92B11ED21.title": "&dThe Odd Ones",
  "quest.5F14BE199B3484CF.quest_desc": [
    "Generation is spiky and demand isn't, so you need a buffer between them.",
    "",
    "Craft any energy storage block. It soaks up the surplus while your machines sit idle and hands it back when they all start at once.",
    "",
    "A Starter &aEnergy Cell&r from &ePowah&r holds 1,000,000 FE, and its Nitro cell holds 2,000,000,000. Every tech mod has its own ladder, so pick the one whose parts you already make.",
    "",
    "&7&oSize your buffer to your biggest single draw, not your average one.&r",
  ],
  "task.6D28CCC2CA870236.title": "Any End-Game Solar Panel",
  "task.19D309213D852B2D.title": "Any Energy Cable, Conduit or Pipe",
  "quest.334613FB40021822.title": "&6Better Burners",
  "task.2B8F534F3694285E.title": "Any Reactor",
  "task.5897362AE575635C.title": "Any Animal or Farm Generator",
  "task.56B5B44D10E7EC7A.title": "Any Early Solar Panel",
  "quest.1A964E72CA3B398D.quest_desc": [
    "The top solar panels make more power than many reactors.",
    "",
    "Build an end-game solar panel. They are the most expensive blocks in this chapter, and they still never need fuel or coolant.",
    "",
    "An &aEV Solar Panel&r makes 16,384 FE/t and needs &2Antimatter&r, which takes a Nether Star and a lot of power to make. &eEnergized Power&r's Tier VII makes 16,000 FE/t, and &ePowah&r's Nitro panel makes 1,024.",
  ],
  "quest.666CC5BD7E85A79A.title": "&2Horse Power",
  "quest.334613FB40021822.quest_desc": [
    "Your first fuel generator is starting to look small.",
    "",
    "Build a mid-game fuel generator. These make several times the power of a day-one burner, and some of them take fluids you can pipe in:",
    "",
    "- &aSimple Fuel Generator&r: 960 FE/t on &eJust Dire Things&r' refined Blaze Ember Fuel.",
    "",
    "- &aCombustion Dynamo&r: 320 FE/t on oil and water, 480 with Redstone added.",
    "",
    "- &aBio Generator&r: 256 RF/t on &eOritech&r biomass.",
    "",
    "- &aFurnator&r: 128 FE/t at Hardened and 256 at Blazing.",
    "",
    "- &aSoul Engine&r: 44 to 100 FE/t from a bound mob soul and the fluid it likes.",
  ],
}